course: dictionary
lesson: 7853
title: Radium: a glowing metal with a hidden danger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Radium is a rare metal element with the symbol Ra. The word radioactive is your clue: radium gives off radiation, and that radiation can harm the body.
explain: «Marie Curie discovered two new elements, polonium and radium.» The sentence tells you who found radium. Marie Curie was a scientist, and she won two Nobel Prizes, one in physics and one in chemistry.
explain: Radium looks magical because it glows faintly in the dark. But the glow is a warning. People once put radium in watch paint, toothpaste and drinks, not knowing it was harmful. Something that looks magical can still be dangerous.
fact: Radium is a rare, radioactive metal element with the symbol Ra.
fact: Radium gives off dangerous radiation and glows faintly in the dark.
fact: Marie and Pierre Curie discovered radium, and Marie Curie separated tiny amounts of it from tonnes of ore.
fact: The Radium Girls were women who painted glowing watch faces and became very ill.
fact: Marie Curie's notebooks are still radioactive, so they are kept in lead-lined boxes.
exercise: Radium is a «rare, radioactive metal element». What does radioactive mean? | It floats on water | It is good for your teeth | *It gives off radiation
exercise: «Marie Curie discovered two new elements, polonium and radium.» Find and copy one word that names a metal element. | discovered | Marie | *radium | new
exercise: Why is radium called a warning story? | It is safe to swallow, so people use it in drinks | It was used to make the sun shine | *People once put it in toothpaste and drinks without knowing it was harmful
test: «Marie Curie was the first person to win two Nobel Prizes, in two different sciences.» What does two different sciences mean? | *Two different subjects, such as physics and chemistry | Two prizes in the same subject | A prize for two people
test: Radium «glows faintly in the dark». What does faintly mean? | *Gives a weak light | Shines very brightly | Makes a loud noise
exam: Why is radium a metal to be careful with, even though it glows? | It is a kind of sweet that is safe to eat | It is a plant that grows in the sun | *It glows in the dark, but it gives off dangerous radiation
